   "response_text": "All 28 range/clamp tests pass.\n\n## Summary\n\n**Cause:** `IntRange._clamp` in `src/click/types.py` ignored the `dir` argument entirely \u2014 for an open bound it returned `bound` unchanged, so clamping to an open max returned the excluded `max`, and to an open min returned the excluded `min`.\n\n**Fix:**\n```python\ndef _clamp(self, bound: int, dir, open: bool) -> int:\n    if not open:\n        return bound\n    # An open bound is not itself part of the range, so move one\n    # integer step inward to land on the nearest valid value.\n    return bound + dir\n```\n`dir` is `-1` when clamping down to `max` and `+1` when clamping up to `min`, so an open max clamps to `max - 1` (15 \u2192 9) and an open min to `min + 1` (-5 \u2192 1). Closed bounds still return `bound` itself (15 \u2192 10, -5 \u2192 0), and in-range values are untouched.\n\nOnly the library source file was modified; no test files were added, edited, or deleted.\n\nDONE",
